    "response": " To solve the problem of loan amplitude, we need to use the formula for the monthly payment of an amortized loan, which is given by:\n\n\\[ M = P \\frac{r(1+r)^n}{(1+r)^n-1} \\]\n\nwhere:\n- \\( M \\) is the monthly payment,\n- \\( P \\) is the principal loan amount ($18,000),\n- \\( r \\) is the monthly interest rate (6.6% annual interest rate divided by 12 months),\n- \\( n \\) is the total number of payments (4 years times 12 months per year).\n\nFirst, we calculate the monthly interest rate \\( r \\):\n\n\\[ r = \\frac{6.6\\%}{12} = \\frac{0.066}{12} = 0.0055 \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the total number of payments \\( n \\):\n\n\\[ n = 4 \\times 12 = 48 \\]\n\nNow, we substitute \\( P = 18000 \\), \\( r = 0.0055 \\), and \\( n = 48 \\) into the formula for the monthly payment:\n\n\\[ M = 18000 \\frac{0.0055(1+0.0055)^{48}}{(1+0.0055)^{48}-1} \\]\n\nFirst, we calculate \\( (1+0.0055)^{48} \\):\n\n\\[ (1+0.0055)^{48} \\approx 1.28336 \\]\n\nNow, we substitute this value back into the formula:\n\n\\[ M = 18000 \\frac{0.0055 \\times 1.28336}{1.28336 - 1} = 18000 \\frac{0.00705848}{0.28336} \\approx 18000 \\times 0.024907 \\approx 448.33 \\]\n\nSo, the monthly payment is approximately $448.33.\n\nNext, we need to find the remaining balance after 18 payments. The formula for the remaining balance \\( B \\) after \\( k \\) payments is:\n\n\\[ B = P \\left( \\frac{(1+r)^n - (1+r)^k}{(1+r)^n - 1} \\right) \\]\n\nwhere \\( k = 18 \\). Substituting the values we have:\n\n\\[ B = 18000 \\left( \\frac{(1+0.0055)^{48} - (1+0.0055)^{18}}{(1+0.0055)^{48} - 1} \\right) \\]\n\nWe already know that \\( (1+0.0055)^{48} \\approx 1.28336 \\). Now, we calculate \\( (1+0.0055)^{18} \\):\n\n\\[ (1+0.0055)^{18} \\approx 1.10251 \\]\n\nSubstituting these values back into the formula:\n\n\\[ B = 18000 \\left( \\frac{1.28336 - 1.10251}{1.28336 - 1} \\right) = 18000 \\left( \\frac{0.18085}{0.28336} \\right) \\approx 18000 \\times 0.6374 \\approx 11473.20 \\]\n\nSo, the remaining balance after 18 payments is approximately $11,473.20.\n\nThe final answers are:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{448.33} \\]\n\\[ \\boxed{11473.20} \\]",
